{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>The cherubim and the flame of the revolving sword.</b> After He drove him from there, He established in that spirit that was in it — the tree of life — the cherubim, which are angels of destruction, and the dread of Elohim which He designated by the flame of the sword, so that they would be a dividing partition between the tree of life and the man. And observe how it says ״את להט החרב״ — 'the flame of the sword' — and did not say את חרב המתהפכת — 'the revolving sword.' For it is known that the flame (להט) has no substance of its own, but is an accident borne by the sword, and it terrifies all who look upon it, and all who see it fear death when they behold it. And the intention is that the Holy One, blessed be He, set preventive causes before the man so that he would not reach the tree of life, in order that His decree not be nullified. And it is possible to interpret that the cherubim are the angels appointed over the seven chambers of Gehenna — and thus the minimum of כרובים is two, and with the letter ה the total is seven — and the verse will mean: the cherubim appointed over להט החרב המתהפכת, for להט is Gehenna, in which the wicked are turned over like meat in a pot. And so our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: להט — this is Gehenna, and the place of judgment. As it is written (Malachi 3:19): ״ולהט אותם וגו'״. And it is known that the angels and Gehenna were created before the earthly Garden of Eden, for the angels and Gehenna were created on the second day, and the earthly Garden of Eden on the third day. And man has the power to overcome them through the fulfillment of the commandments, and they will be no partition between him and the tree of life at all, but he will draw near and live forever." "<b>Furthermore,</b> you shall know and understand from the meaning of this verse: את הכרובים — they are the holy living creatures (חיות הקדש), as it is written (Ezekiel 10:20): ״היא החיה אשר ראיתי וגו' ואדע כי כרובים המה״. And it is known that each living creature (חיה) has sixteen faces — four to each direction of the four directions of the world, from what is written ״וד' פנים לאחת״ — this applies to each living creature, and likewise to each face — and so they are sixteen faces for each living creature. And these cherubim are the flaming thing borne by the revolving sword; this is what it says: ״ואת להט החרב המתהפכת״ — it is the living creature of the Holy One, blessed be He, which has sixteen faces, and it is the attribute of His judgment. And set all your heart on how He called them להט (flame), which is a thing borne by the sword, and the sword bears it — for so the holy living creatures, even though they appear to bear the Glory, the Glory bears them. And you already know that they are hinted at in the four letters of the Name, which are the beginning of the Intellects, and the tenth rung is hinted at by the יו״ד at the beginning of the Name, and what remains in the Name equals the number of faces that each living creature has — sixteen faces — which shield him from the revolving sword. And they are cut for us in the Torah, in which it is written ״עץ חיים היא״ — it has sixteen covenants corresponding to them: thirteen in the covenant of circumcision and three in the reception of the Torah, and through them we are saved from the sword of the Holy One, blessed be He — the attribute of His judgment above, concerning which it is said: it walks among the living creatures."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {1 "The phrase 'היא מתהלכת בין החיות' at the end of comment 1 appears to be an allusion to Habakkuk 3:5 read through an Ezekiel-chariot lens, or possibly a near-quotation whose exact biblical source is uncertain; rendered hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:10:09.068609886Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}